===Independent on-chain validation of all three pairs===

Reviewers can re-run an end-to-end audit of every commit/reveal pair listed above without trusting any libdogecoin code path.  The committed driver <code>contrib/zk_carrier/scripts/validate_onchain_pairs.py</code>:

# fetches each TX_C / TX_R as raw hex from a public block explorer (default <code>api.blockchair.com/dogecoin</code>; override via <code>EXPLORER=</code>);
# parses the transaction in pure Python (no libdogecoin) and decodes the <code>OP_RETURN "DZKC" || mode || commit32</code> output of TX_C;
# walks every TX_R input, decodes the chunked <code>ZKP1FULL</code> carrier scriptSigs (tag8 / 8-byte header / three ≤520 B chunks / redeem), reorders parts by <code>part_idx</code> and reassembles the canonical ZKP1 payload;
# computes <code>SHA256d(payload)</code> and asserts it equals the on-chain <code>commit32</code>;
# decodes the big-endian ZKP1 wire format (mode / circuit_id / public_len / proof_len) and asserts the embedded <code>proof.protocol</code> matches the committed mode (<code>groth16</code> for mode=0, <code>plonk</code> for mode=1);
# invokes <code>snarkjs ${system} verify</code> against the in-tree <code>verification_key.json</code> / <code>verification_key_plonk.json</code> as the cryptographic ground truth.

