The <code>PASS</code> line for Pair G1 / Pair Q1 is the strongest possible on-chain claim this BIP can make: every byte that the verifier consumes — <code>public_inputs</code>, <code>proof</code>, AND <code>vk</code> — was recovered from a single TX_R reveal and bound back to the matching TX_C commit by <code>SHA256d</code>; no out-of-band file or registry was consulted at any step. <code>snarkjs</code> is the canonical reference verifier for both Groth16 and PLONK proofs; an equivalent <code>spvnode</code> verdict can be obtained by rebuilding libdogecoin with <code>HAVE_RAPIDSNARK</code> and the <code>--zk-vkey-from-reveal</code> mode (planned for the next phase).

